{"name":"Dancing Bear","hex":"#94734c","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dancing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The activity of taking part in a dance.","A dance club in France."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of dance"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dancing"},{"term":"bear","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, generally omnivorous mammal (a few species are purely carnivorous or herbivorous) of the family Ursidae; having shaggy fur, a very small tail, and flat feet.","A rough, unmannerly, uncouth person. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To endeavour to depress the price of, or prices in."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bear"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dancing Bear","blocks":[{"text":"Dancing Bear is a Croatian record label."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dancing_Bear","wikidata":"Q3115913"},{"title":"Tame bear","blocks":[{"text":"A tame bear, often called a dancing bear, is a wild bear captured when young or born and bred in captivity. These bears have been used to entertain people in streets or taverns. Dancing bears were commonplace throughout Europe and Asia from the Middle Ages to the 19th century, and can still be found in the 21st century in some countries. In these countries, organizations and animal rights activists have sought to eliminate the practice, citing the mistreatment and abuse used to train the bears."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/The_dancing_bear_by_William_Frederick_Witherington.jpg/330px-The_dancing_bear_by_William_Frederick_Witherington.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tame_bear","wikidata":"Q1641981"},{"title":"Bear","blocks":[{"text":"Bears are carnivoran mammals of the family Ursidae. They are classified as caniforms within the suborder Caniformia. Although only eight species of bears are extant, they are widespread, appearing in a wide variety of habitats throughout most of the Northern Hemisphere and partially in the Southern Hemisphere. Bears are found on the continents of North America, South America, and Eurasia. Common characteristics of modern bears include large bodies with stocky legs, long snouts, small rounded ears, shaggy hair, plantigrade paws with five nonretractile claws, and short tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg/330px-Ours_brun_parcanimalierpyrenees_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear","wikidata":"Q11788"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/The_dancing_bear_by_William_Frederick_Witherington.jpg/500px-The_dancing_bear_by_William_Frederick_Witherington.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/The_dancing_bear_by_William_Frederick_Witherington.jpg/500px-The_dancing_bear_by_William_Frederick_Witherington.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The dancing bear by William Frederick Witherington, England, 1822","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_dancing_bear_by_William_Frederick_Witherington.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Dancing_bear_by_Olearius_%281883323%29.jpg/250px-Dancing_bear_by_Olearius_%281883323%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Dancing_bear_by_Olearius_%281883323%29.jpg/500px-Dancing_bear_by_Olearius_%281883323%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Dancing_bear_by_Olearius_%281883323%